> {{ site.title }}: {{ site.subtitle }} is a self-help and personal-development book by {{ site.author }}. It makes the case for caring deeply about fewer things and letting the rest go on purpose: the Joy of Missing Out (JOMO) reframed as a deliberate way of choosing, working, and living amid infinite options and AI-era pressure. Available as a Kindle edition (ASIN {{ site.book.kindle.asin }}, {{ site.book.kindle.numberOfPages }} pages){% if site.book.paperback.asin %} and a paperback (ASIN {{ site.book.paperback.asin }}, ISBN {{ site.book.paperback.isbn }}, {{ site.book.paperback.numberOfPages }} pages){% endif %}, published {{ site.book.datePublished }}. Full and fulfilling are two different things; this book is the case for choosing the second.

