## What it covers
- The difference between a life that is full and one that is fulfilling.
- The paradox of choice: why more options have quietly made us less happy.
- The three types of no: the hard no, the soft no, and the structural no.
- One-thing seasons: going deep on one thing instead of skimming a dozen half-finished projects.
- The five per cent shift: JOMO for people who cannot simply walk away.
- Why saying no can feel physically hard (social pain), and how to reframe it.
- Breaking the grip of comparison by curating what you allow into your head.
- Turning a life that is merely full into one that is genuinely fulfilling.

